# `-d ovh` only — the OVH prod-like test box. Read as [.kamal/secrets-common, .kamal/secrets.ovh];
# .kamal/secrets (base) is NOT read. Safe for git: references and commands only, never a raw
# credential.
#
# CHUNK_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY AND CHUNK_ACCESS_KEY_ID WERE HERE — the Cloudflare R2 token and access
# key id, from when the maker app resolved a chunk store of its own. Arc D Part 2 handed the chunk
# store to the `sync` accessory (chaim354/tinkerex-sync, its own env), and nothing in this repo has
# read STORAGE_BACKEND or any CHUNK_* storage knob since (§7, §14a) — so both names were dead. Dead
# in a secrets file is NOT free: Kamal's InlineCommandSubstitution runs every `$(…)` in a parsed
# file EAGERLY rather than lazily per key, so each was a 1Password read on every `-d ovh` deploy for
# a value no container consumed. THE 1PASSWORD ITEMS THEY POINTED AT ARE STILL LIVE AND ARE NOW READ
# UNDER THEIR REAL NAMES BELOW: the backend decision landed on `s3`, so the same R2 credential that
# used to sign chunk URLs now signs library URLs.
#
# ⚠️ THE OLD NAMES WERE SHARED WITH THE UNRAID LEGS WHILE THE CREDENTIALS WERE NOT — R2 here,
# SeaweedFS in .kamal/secrets — which is why they could never have lived in secrets-common. THE
# SAME TRAP APPLIES TO THE TWO LINES BELOW, and is the reason they are here rather than there:
# .kamal/secrets.s3 resolves LIBRARY_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY to `op://tinkerex/seaweednew/secret key`
# for the Unraid leg. One variable name, two backends, two credentials — secrets-common could not
# tell them apart, and a destination reading the wrong one signs with InvalidAccessKeyId
# (docs/invariants/deploy-secrets.md, §14g).

# THE R2 CREDENTIAL PAIR FOR THIS BOX'S LIBRARY (LIBRARY_BACKEND=s3, see config/deploy.ovh.yml).
# BOTH ARE env.secret, INCLUDING THE ACCESS KEY ID, AND THAT DIFFERS FROM deploy.s3.yml ON PURPOSE:
# the Unraid leg carries its key id in env.clear because an access key ID is an identifier rather
# than a credential, and that is still true here — but a value defined in a secrets file is NEVER
# visible to ERB in env.clear (see the tombstone in config/deploy.ovh.yml), and putting the literal
# in clear is what this destination already tried once and reverted. env.secret costs one extra
# vault read and needs no literal in git.
LIBRARY_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=$(bin/secret LIBRARY_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID 'op://tinkerex/R2/access key id')
LIBRARY_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=$(bin/secret LIBRARY_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY 'op://tinkerex/R2/secret access key')

# SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN — this destination's own app never SENDS it: it declares LIBRARY_BACKEND=s3, and
# only a chunk_remote app calls FileLayer::ChunkRemote::Provisioning's admin door. Required here
# anyway, and structurally rather than by choice:
# the `sync` accessory (config/deploy.yml, Arc D Task 2) declares SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN as ITS OWN
# secret, and `accessories:` is never overridden by a destination overlay — so it folds into EVERY
# destination's merged config, this one included. Verified against Kamal::Configuration.raw_config,
# not assumed; test/deploy_hygiene_test.rb re-derives it on every run. NOT in secrets-common, on
# explicit instruction (§14g; unlike SECRET_KEY_BASE, which is — see that file's own comment).
# The fullest version of this argument lives with the accessory itself, in config/deploy.yml.
SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN=$(bin/secret SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN 'op://tinkerex/tinkerex-sync-admin-token/password')

# THE CLOUDFLARE ORIGIN CERTIFICATE FOR kamal-proxy (config/deploy.ovh.yml `proxy: ssl:`). Both
# values are multi-line PEMs: bin/secret prints them verbatim (`printf '%s'`) and Kamal's
# InlineCommandSubstitution keeps everything but the trailing newline, so they survive the dotenv
# parse intact. Not in secrets-common: no other destination terminates TLS (the Unraid legs are
# plain HTTP behind the NPM front proxy). Item fields measured 2026-10-12: `certificate` and
# `private key`, SANs tinkerex.com + *.tinkerex.com, valid to 2041.
OVH_ORIGIN_CERTIFICATE_PEM=$(bin/secret OVH_ORIGIN_CERTIFICATE_PEM 'op://tinkerex/tinkerex-origin/certificate')
OVH_ORIGIN_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM=$(bin/secret OVH_ORIGIN_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM 'op://tinkerex/tinkerex-origin/private key')
